{"book":"PSA","chapter":70,"source":"hbo","verses":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"records":[{"id":"PSA.70.1.s1","verses":[1],"source":"לַ֝מְנַצֵּ֗חַ לְדָוִ֥ד לְהַזְכִּֽיר׃","gloss":"For the director. Of David. To bring to remembrance.","pieces":[[1,"For the music director. Of David. For remembrance.",null]],"L":{"1":"For the director: of David; to bring to remembrance."},"R":{"1":"For the leader of the music. By David. To call to mind."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"punctuation","tokens":["o190700010011","o190700010012","o190700010021","o190700010022","o190700010031","o190700010032"],"choice":"The title is verse 1","alternatives":[],"reason":"The title is part of the Hebrew text and is counted as verse 1, so the verse numbers here are one higher than in Bibles that print the title without a number.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190700010012"],"choice":"the director","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 4:1.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190700010031","o190700010032"],"choice":"to bring to remembrance: to call to mind before God","alternatives":["for the memorial offering","to remind"],"reason":"As in 38:1, the only other psalm with this heading. The psalm may call the sufferer's need to God's mind, or may have been sung with the \"memorial portion\" of the grain offering ('azkarah, Leviticus 2:2), a word from the same root.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m4","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o190700010032"],"choice":"Psalm 70 is Psalm 40:14-18","alternatives":[],"reason":"Verses 2-6 repeat Psalm 40:14-18 with small changes: several times \"God\" stands where Psalm 40 has the divine name, and the other way round in verse 6. Psalms 42-83 often use \"God\" ('elohim) where other psalms use the name, and each level here follows the word this psalm has.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190700010022","o190700010032"],"choice":"By David; To call to mind","alternatives":["Of David; To bring to remembrance"],"reason":"Readable uses plain words, as in 38:1; the sense of the phrase is uncertain (m3).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":"Hurry, God, and help me","status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.70.2.s1","verses":[2],"source":"אֱלֹהִ֥ים לְהַצִּילֵ֑נִי יְ֝הוָ֗ה לְעֶזְרָ֥תִי חֽוּשָֽׁה׃","gloss":"God, to deliver me; YHWH, to my help hurry.","pieces":[[2,"God, come and rescue me! \\q {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, be quick to help me!",null]],"L":{"2":"God, [come] to rescue me; \\q {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, hurry to my help!"},"R":{"2":"God, come and save me! \\q {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, hurry and help me!"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o190700020011","o190700020022"],"choice":"God, to deliver me: a cry with the verb left out","alternatives":["God, be pleased to deliver me (Psalm 40:14)"],"reason":"The first line has no main verb, only \"to deliver me\". Psalm 40:14 begins \"Be pleased, YHWH, to deliver me\"; here the urgent cry is shorter, and \"hurry\" at the end of the verse governs both halves.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o190700020011","o190700020031"],"choice":"Psalm 40:14","alternatives":[],"reason":"This verse matches Psalm 40:14, with \"God\" in place of the first \"YHWH\".","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["L","B","R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o190700020022"],"choice":"come","alternatives":[],"reason":"The cry lacks a verb; \"come\" is supplied from the sense and from \"hurry\" in the second half. Literal marks it with brackets.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.70.3.s1","verses":[3],"source":"יֵבֹ֣שׁוּ וְיַחְפְּרוּ֮ מְבַקְשֵׁ֪י נַ֫פְשִׁ֥י יִסֹּ֣גוּ אָ֭חוֹר וְיִכָּלְמ֑וּ חֲ֝פֵצֵ֗י רָעָתִֽי׃","gloss":"May they be ashamed and abashed, those who seek my life; may they be turned back and humiliated, those who desire my harm.","pieces":[[3,"Let those who are out to take my life be shamed and confounded; \\q let those who want me hurt be driven back in disgrace.",null]],"L":{"3":"May they be ashamed and abashed, those who seek my life; \\q may they be turned back and humiliated, \\q those who desire my harm."},"R":{"3":"Some people want me dead. Let them be ashamed and confused. \\q Some people want to see me hurt. \\q Make them turn away in shame."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o190700030011","o190700030072"],"choice":"may they be ashamed: a prayer against enemies","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verbs are wishes: that the enemies' plans fail and the shame they meant for him falls on them (35:4, 26; 40:15).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o190700030031","o190700030041"],"choice":"seek my life: try to kill me","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 40:15, which adds \"to snatch it away\" and \"together\"; this verse is shorter.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190700030011","o190700030051"],"choice":"Let them ... Make them ...","alternatives":["May they be ..."],"reason":"Readable puts the wishes as plain requests, with the enemies named first.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.70.4.s1","verses":[4],"source":"יָ֭שׁוּבוּ עַל־עֵ֣קֶב בָּשְׁתָּ֑ם הָ֝אֹמְרִ֗ים הֶ֘אָ֥ח׀הֶאָֽח׃","gloss":"May they turn back on account of their shame, those who say, Aha, aha!","pieces":[[4,"Let those who crow \"Aha! Aha!\" \\q retreat because of their own disgrace.",null]],"L":{"4":"May they turn back on account of their shame, \\q those who say, \"Aha! Aha!\""},"R":{"4":"Some people laugh and say, \"Ha! Ha!\" \\q Let them run away because they are put to shame."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o190700040061","o190700040071"],"choice":"Aha, aha: a gloating laugh","alternatives":[],"reason":"The cry is the glee of enemies at someone's fall (35:21, 25; 40:16).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190700040011"],"choice":"turn back: retreat, as an army turns and runs","alternatives":["be appalled (Psalm 40:16)"],"reason":"Psalm 40:16 has \"be appalled\" (shamem); this verse has \"turn back\" (shuv), repeating the picture of defeat from verse 3.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190700040031","o190700040041"],"choice":"on account of their shame: as the result of it","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word ('eqev) means \"as the consequence of\": their own shame drives them off.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.70.5.s1","verses":[5],"source":"יָ֘שִׂ֤ישׂוּ וְיִשְׂמְח֨וּ׀בְּךָ֗ כָּֽל־מְבַ֫קְשֶׁ֥יךָ וְיֹאמְר֣וּ תָ֭מִיד יִגְדַּ֣ל אֱלֹהִ֑ים אֹ֝הֲבֵ֗י יְשׁוּעָתֶֽךָ׃","gloss":"May they exult and rejoice in you, all who seek you; and may they say continually, Great [is] God, those who love your salvation.","pieces":[[5,"But may all who look for {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} be glad and take delight in {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}, \\q and let all who love {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} saving help keep saying, \"God is great!\"",null]],"L":{"5":"May they exult and rejoice in {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}, all who seek {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}; \\q and may they say continually, \"Great [is] God!\" \\q those who love {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} salvation."},"R":{"5":"But let all who come to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} be happy and full of joy because of {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}. \\q Let all who love it when {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} save them say again and again, \"God is great!\""},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o190700050081","o190700050091"],"choice":"Great is God: praise, or a wish","alternatives":["May God be magnified!"],"reason":"The verb can be read as a wish, \"may God be great\", that is, be shown and praised as great. Psalm 40:17 has the divine name here.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190700050051","o190700050052"],"choice":"those who seek you: those who turn to God in worship and prayer","alternatives":[],"reason":"To seek God is to come to him for help and to worship him (9:11; 24:6).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["B","R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o190700050011"],"choice":"But","alternatives":[],"reason":"The wish for those who seek God is set against the wish for the enemies.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.70.6.s1","verses":[6],"source":"וַאֲנִ֤י׀עָנִ֣י וְאֶבְיוֹן֮ אֱלֹהִ֪ים חֽוּשָׁ֫ה־לִּ֥י עֶזְרִ֣י וּמְפַלְטִ֣י אַ֑תָּה יְ֝הוָ֗ה אַל־תְּאַחַֽר׃","gloss":"And I [am] afflicted and needy; God, hurry to me; my help and my deliverer [are] you; YHWH, do not delay.","pieces":[[6,"As for me, I am poor and in need; God, come to me quickly! \\q You are my helper and the one who sets me free; \\q {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, do not hold back!",null]],"L":{"6":"But I [am] poor and needy; God, hurry to me! \\q My help and my deliverer [are] {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}; \\q {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, do not delay!"},"R":{"6":"I am poor and I have nothing. God, come to me quickly! \\q You are the one who helps me and saves me. \\q {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, please do not wait!"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190700060021","o190700060032"],"choice":"afflicted and needy: helpless and dependent on God","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 40:18; the pair describes those who have no help but God.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o190700060041","o190700060051","o190700060101"],"choice":"Psalm 40:18","alternatives":[],"reason":"Psalm 40:18 has \"the Lord will think of me\" where this verse has \"God, hurry to me\", and \"my God\" where this verse has the divine name. The psalm ends as it began, with \"hurry\" (verse 2).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"}],"words":{"1":[{"id":"o190700010011","text":"לַ֝","after":"","lemma":"לְ","morph":"Rd","gloss":"to","strong":"3807a","transliteration":"la","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition · with the article"},{"id":"o190700010012","text":"מְנַצֵּ֗חַ","after":" ","lemma":"נָצַח","morph":"Vprmsa","gloss":"choirmaster","strong":"5329","transliteration":"mənaṣṣēᵃḥ","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Piel · participle · masculine singular absolute"},{"id":"o190700010021","text":"לְ","after":"","lemma":"לְ","morph":"R","gloss":"of","strong":"3807a","transliteration":"lə","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition"},{"id":"o190700010022","text":"דָוִ֥ד","after":" ","lemma":"דָּוִד","morph":"Np","gloss":"David","strong":"1732","transliteration":"ḏāwiḏ","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · proper name"},{"id":"o190700010031","text":"לְ","after":"","lemma":"לְ","morph":"R","gloss":"to","strong":"3807a","transliteration":"lə","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition"},{"id":"o190700010032","text":"הַזְכִּֽיר","after":"׃","lemma":"זָכַר","morph":"Vhc","gloss":"make.remembrance","strong":"2142","transliteration":"hazkiyr:","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Hiphil · infinitive construct"}],"2":[{"id":"o190700020011","text":"אֱלֹהִ֥ים","after":" ","lemma":"אֱלֹהִים","morph":"Ncmpa","gloss":"O.God","strong":"0430","transli